IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`

-- je21-tests-art02-making: tests for Article 2 (Making of Jersey Legislation).
-- The expected values were written by hand from Article 2 before the module was run.
-- Both texts of Article 2(1) are tested with the same scenarios, because the endnotes record nothing but the wording of (b) changing (see NOTES.md section 5).

§ `Article 2 -- tests`

§§ `Names for the readings (the first of each pair is the default)`

`L4 registration` MEANS `the day it was registered, by Article 2(4)`
`L4 latest step` MEANS `the latest of the days on which the three steps of Article 2(1) were done`
`L8 declaration` MEANS `the declaration by Act of the States is all that Article 2(2) requires`
`L8 adoption too` MEANS `the taxation draft must also have been adopted by the States Assembly, which Article 2(2) does not excuse`

§§ `Laws`

--                                                          adopted                     sanctioned                   registered                  taxation draft
`a Law with the three steps done in order`      MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 5 1), JUST (YMD 2022 6 15), JUST (YMD 2022 6 17), FALSE
`a Law registered before it was sanctioned`     MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 5 1), JUST (YMD 2022 6 15), JUST (YMD 2022 6 10), FALSE
`a Law adopted last, registered first`          MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 7 1), JUST (YMD 2022 6 15), JUST (YMD 2022 6 10), FALSE
`a Law not adopted`                             MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF NOTHING,             JUST (YMD 2022 6 15), JUST (YMD 2022 6 17), FALSE
`a Law not sanctioned`                          MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 5 1), NOTHING,              JUST (YMD 2022 6 17), FALSE
`a Law not registered`                          MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 5 1), JUST (YMD 2022 6 15), NOTHING,              FALSE
`a taxation draft declared and adopted only`    MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 5 1), NOTHING,              NOTHING,              TRUE
`a taxation draft declared and nothing else`    MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF NOTHING,             NOTHING,              NOTHING,              TRUE
`a taxation draft with all three steps done`    MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 5 1), JUST (YMD 2022 6 15), JUST (YMD 2022 6 17), TRUE
`a draft adopted but not declared`              MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 5 1), NOTHING,              NOTHING,              FALSE

§§ `2(1) in the text of 28 September 2021`

#ASSERT `Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law with the three steps done in order`
#ASSERT `Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law registered before it was sanctioned`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law not adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law not sanctioned`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law not registered`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 28 September 2021): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a taxation draft declared and adopted only`

§§ `2(1) in the text of 11 January 2024`

#ASSERT `Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law with the three steps done in order`
#ASSERT `Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law registered before it was sanctioned`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law not adopted`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law not sanctioned`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a Law not registered`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(1) (text of 11 January 2024): all three steps of making a Law have been done` `a taxation draft declared and adopted only`

§§ `2(2) A taxation draft`

#ASSERT `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` `a taxation draft declared and adopted only` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` `a taxation draft declared and adopted only` `L8 adoption too`
#ASSERT `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L8 adoption too`
-- Not a taxation draft declared by Act: Article 2(2) does not apply, whatever else is done.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` `a draft adopted but not declared` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(2): the taxation draft is treated as having been made as a Law` `a Law with the three steps done in order` `L8 declaration`

§§ `Whether a Law has been made, under each text`

#ASSERT `Article 2 (text of 28 September 2021): the Law has been made` `a Law with the three steps done in order` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT `Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` `a Law with the three steps done in order` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 (text of 28 September 2021): the Law has been made` `a Law not registered` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` `a Law not registered` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 (text of 28 September 2021): the Law has been made` `a Law not adopted` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` `a Law not sanctioned` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT `Article 2 (text of 28 September 2021): the Law has been made` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT `Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L8 declaration`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 (text of 28 September 2021): the Law has been made` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L8 adoption too`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L8 adoption too`
#ASSERT `Article 2 (text of 11 January 2024): the Law has been made` `a taxation draft with all three steps done` `L8 adoption too`

§§ `2(4) The day a Law was made`

-- Steps in order: registration is the last step, and both readings of L4 give the day of registration.
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law with the three steps done in order` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 6 17)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law with the three steps done in order` `L4 latest step` `L8 declaration` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 6 17)
-- Registered before it was sanctioned: the readings differ. The default is the day of registration (10 June), the other reading is the day of the last step (15 June).
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law registered before it was sanctioned` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 6 10)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law registered before it was sanctioned` `L4 latest step` `L8 declaration` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 6 15)
-- Adopted last: the last step is adoption, 1 July.
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law adopted last, registered first` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 6 10)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law adopted last, registered first` `L4 latest step` `L8 declaration` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 7 1)
-- A step missing and no deeming: the Law has not been made, so there is no day.
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law not adopted` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law not sanctioned` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a Law not registered` `L4 latest step` `L8 declaration` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a draft adopted but not declared` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A taxation draft treated as made without the steps: the Law does not say on what day.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a taxation draft declared and adopted only` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` BECAUSE "Article 2(2) treats a taxation draft as made without the steps of Article 2(1)(b) and (c) and does not say on what day it was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` BECAUSE "Article 2(2) treats a taxation draft as made without the steps of Article 2(1)(b) and (c) and does not say on what day it was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a taxation draft declared and adopted only` `L4 registration` `L8 adoption too` BECAUSE "Article 2(2) treats a taxation draft as made without the steps of Article 2(1)(b) and (c) and does not say on what day it was made"
-- On the reading that adoption is also needed, a taxation draft that was never adopted is not made, so there is no day.
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a taxation draft declared and nothing else` `L4 registration` `L8 adoption too` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A taxation draft that did complete all three steps is made by Article 2(1), on the day of registration.
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the Law was made` `a taxation draft with all three steps done` `L4 registration` `L8 declaration` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2022 6 17)

§§ `Subordinate legislation`

--                                                                          form                                              adopted                  signed on                signed by the person responsible  by a body  per procedure
`Regulations adopted on 7 March 2023`                    MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `Regulations`,                                      JUST (YMD 2023 3 7),     NOTHING,                 FALSE,                            FALSE,     FALSE
`Regulations signed but not adopted`                     MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `Regulations`,                                      NOTHING,                 JUST (YMD 2023 3 8),     TRUE,                             FALSE,     FALSE
`Triennial Regulations adopted on 1 April 2023`          MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `Triennial Regulations`,                            JUST (YMD 2023 4 1),     NOTHING,                 FALSE,                            FALSE,     FALSE
`an Act adopted on 2 May 2023`                           MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation`,  JUST (YMD 2023 5 2),     NOTHING,                 FALSE,                            FALSE,     FALSE
`an Act not adopted`                                     MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation`,  NOTHING,                 NOTHING,                 FALSE,                            FALSE,     FALSE
`an Order signed by the person responsible on 9 May 2023` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`,                                         NOTHING,                 JUST (YMD 2023 5 9),     TRUE,                             FALSE,     FALSE
`an Order of a body signed in accordance with its procedure` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`,                                      NOTHING,                 JUST (YMD 2023 5 10),    FALSE,                            TRUE,      TRUE
`an Order of a body signed against its procedure`        MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`,                                         NOTHING,                 JUST (YMD 2023 5 10),    FALSE,                            TRUE,      FALSE
`an Order signed by no one entitled`                     MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`,                                         NOTHING,                 JUST (YMD 2023 5 10),    FALSE,                            FALSE,     FALSE
`an Order whose signer followed procedure but it is not a body` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`,                                  NOTHING,                 JUST (YMD 2023 5 10),    FALSE,                            FALSE,     TRUE
`an Order not yet signed`                                MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`,                                         NOTHING,                 NOTHING,                 TRUE,                             FALSE,     FALSE
`another instrument signed by the person responsible on 11 May 2023` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey`, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2023 5 11), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Law described as subordinate legislation`             MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `a Law`,                                            NOTHING,                 NOTHING,                 FALSE,                            FALSE,     FALSE
`UK extended legislation described as subordinate legislation` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `UK extended legislation`,                  NOTHING,                 NOTHING,                 FALSE,                            FALSE,     FALSE

-- 2(3)(a): adoption of the proposition.
#ASSERT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `Regulations adopted on 7 March 2023`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `Regulations signed but not adopted`
#ASSERT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `Triennial Regulations adopted on 1 April 2023`
#ASSERT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Act adopted on 2 May 2023`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Act not adopted`
-- 2(3)(b): signature, by the person responsible or, for a body, by a person acting in accordance with its procedure.
#ASSERT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Order signed by the person responsible on 9 May 2023`
#ASSERT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Order of a body signed in accordance with its procedure`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Order of a body signed against its procedure`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Order signed by no one entitled`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Order whose signer followed procedure but it is not a body`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `an Order not yet signed`
#ASSERT `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `another instrument signed by the person responsible on 11 May 2023`
-- Not subordinate legislation at all.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `a Law described as subordinate legislation` BECAUSE "Article 2(3) is about Jersey subordinate legislation, and a Law is made under Article 2(1)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 2(3): the subordinate legislation has been adopted or signed as the Law requires` `UK extended legislation described as subordinate legislation` BECAUSE "Article 2(3) is about Jersey subordinate legislation, and UK extended legislation is not made under this Law"

§§ `2(4) The day subordinate legislation was made`

#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `Regulations adopted on 7 March 2023` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 3 7)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `Regulations signed but not adopted` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `Triennial Regulations adopted on 1 April 2023` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 4 1)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `an Act adopted on 2 May 2023` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 5 2)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `an Order signed by the person responsible on 9 May 2023` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 5 9)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `an Order of a body signed in accordance with its procedure` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 5 10)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `another instrument signed by the person responsible on 11 May 2023` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 5 11)
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `an Order of a body signed against its procedure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `an Order not yet signed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 2(4): the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` `a Law described as subordinate legislation` BECAUSE "Article 2(3) is about Jersey subordinate legislation, and a Law is made under Article 2(1)"
